  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.repositories.mongodb.models.CatalogItem\": {\n        \"summary\": \"A MongoDB document model class representing a catalog item in the ordering system, mapped to the 'catalog' collection. It serves as a persistence layer entity that bridges the domain model (`smpl.ordering.models.CatalogItem`) and the MongoDB database. Key fields include `id` (MongoDB document identifier annotated with `@Id`), `skuNumber` (indexed for efficient querying, annotated with `@Indexed`), `description`, `price`, `inventory`, and `leadTime`. Key methods include: (1) `CatalogItem(smpl.ordering.models.CatalogItem from)` — a conversion constructor that populates this MongoDB model from a domain model instance; (2) `toCatalogItem()` — converts this MongoDB model back to a domain model instance, applying business logic where `leadTime` is set to 0 if inventory is greater than 0 (item is in stock), otherwise the stored `leadTime` value is used. Standard getters and setters are provided for `id`. This class follows the repository pattern, acting as a Data Transfer Object (DTO) between the application domain layer and MongoDB persistence layer.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/repositories/mongodb/models/CatalogItem.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
